---
/* THE ROUTE `wrangler.jsonc` HAS BEEN POINTING AT SINCE IT WAS WRITTEN.

   `assets.not_found_handling` is already set to `404-page`, which serves the
   nearest `404.html` for anything that does not match a file. There was no
   `404.html`, so the setting resolved to Cloudflare's bare default and the
   four legal links in the footer -- all of which 404'd at the time -- landed
   the reader on an unbranded error with no way back.

   THE LEGAL ROUTES RESOLVE NOW, and one of the four does not exist on purpose:
   `/dpa` was drawn into the footer and then removed rather than written, so a
   link to it survives in somebody's notes and lands here. ../lib/legal carries
   why there is no agreement to put at that address.

   It is `noindex, follow`: reachable, rendered, and never a search result.
   `follow` rather than `nofollow` because the one link on it is the way home,
   and a crawler that arrives here through a stale link should take it. */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base
  title={`Not found | ${SITE.name}`}
  description="This page does not exist."
  noindex
>
  <section class="sec">
    <div class="wrap">
      {/* An `h1` and not the `h2` every other section head carries: this is
          the whole page, not a section of one, and a document whose only
          heading starts at level two is a document a screen reader reports as
          having no title. */}
      <div class="sec__head rise">
        <h1>Nothing at this address.</h1>
        <p>The page you asked for does not exist. If you were looking for the
          legal pages, they are in the footer: the imprint, the privacy notice
          and the terms.</p>
      </div>
      {/* Same `data-back` contract as the legal pages: the href is what it
          is, and the press becomes a `history.back()` only where the index is
          the entry behind this one. Arriving here from a stale link, it is
          not, and the href stands. */}
      <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/" data-back>Back to the start</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
